  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758572,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "Step into the suave and dangerous world of James Bond in *007: The World Is Not Enough* for PlayStation, a first-person shooter based on the thrilling 1999 film. Assume the role of 007 as you embark on 11 action-packed missions, battling enemies and completing objectives ranging from hostage rescues to vehicle destruction. Utilize a full arsenal of Q-Lab gadgets, including the Credit Card Lockpick and Micro Camera, to overcome obstacles and infiltrate enemy strongholds.\n\nDeveloped by Black Ops Entertainment, this game builds upon the foundation of previous Bond titles, featuring improved graphics and a focus on immersive gameplay. While lacking the multiplayer mode found in the Nintendo 64 version, the PlayStation release delivers a compelling single-player experience with authentic dialogue and cinematic cutscenes from the film. Master a variety of weapons, from submachine guns to rocket launchers, and utilize power-ups to survive intense firefights. Experience the intensity of being James Bond – license to thrill awaits!"
    },
